"""Recurring biological compatibility questions, separate from scoring sheets."""

CONTEXT_TASK = """Determine whether the assigned possible function is compatible with the stated organism, strain, biological situation or sample. Keep the question's scope fixed, including whether it asks about the existence of a compatible biological state or the fraction of a defined sample that is compatible. A possible function and organism assignment may emerge from the supplied material; a searchable gene name or initial annotation is not required. Never select the question according to which numerical result is larger.

Use the requirement_compatibility assessment type across organisms, compartments and source formats. For an assessment of one original experiment, record experiment_assessment with the actual received assay reference, a stable assessment_key, scientific question, conclusion and limitations. Corrections to that experiment's assessment keep the same experiment_ref and assessment_key, name the latest revises_sheet_ref and explain the revision_reason. A claim-level assessment combining distinct original experiments uses its source_selection.question binding and preserves separate physical contexts, measurements and source witnesses; the composite is not one of its contributing assays. Several requirements, representations or revised assessments do not become additional experiments. Preserve old source measurements and conclusions in their saved sheets.

Identify the necessary conditions and genuine alternative routes. Preserve measured local values, their physical unit bases, supported and incompatible domains, uncertainty and source limitations. Keep purified-enzyme conditions, culture conditions and habitat measurements separate. Untested values are unresolved, not automatically incompatible. A sufficient dose is not a minimum or a continuous operating interval. Gas volume fraction and dissolved saturation are different quantities; bulk concentration need not be local exposure. A taxon label, structural similarity or an unverified generalization does not supply a measured trait or local mapping.

Support each proposed prerequisite as a requirement of the claimed function. Conditions with a reported positive readout form an observation panel; their complement becomes an incompatible domain only where evidence establishes a necessary exclusion. Preserve negative or undetected readouts with their endpoint and detection or statistical limits. When a missing readout leaves the biological prerequisite open, retain an unresolved relation instead of treating a map of reported positives as complete compatibility coverage.

For every actual requirement, preserve its source-supported definition, entity or substance, property, biological setting and relationship to the investigated function when available. Bind those meanings to that requirement's own unit and supported/incompatible domains; identical units or values do not make requirements equivalent. Preserve each genuine alternative route's source-supported identity, exact required members and support for their joint biological scope. Literal labels and witnesses must match the actual source; legitimate source-supported interpretation need not appear as our terminology verbatim. Leave missing meanings and missing support unknown. Distinct scoped handles for unnamed requirements or routes identify different operands without asserting their substance or independent evidence. Meanings identify operands and qualify interpretation; their absence adds no numerical scoring gate, and supplied domains and relations retain their existing conditional meaning.

Establish which biological situations the evidence actually covers. A verified compatible state can witness capability within its stated scope. A finite list without a witness cannot establish impossibility while permitted situations remain unexamined. Specify actual necessary exclusions and their complete scope before treating a capability as excluded. A purified-enzyme assay alone is not a whole-organism witness, and gene or partner searches remain separate work.

Derive biological requirements from the actual functional claim. Distinguish required circumstances from unresolved details of the molecular mechanism. A source-supported observation of the attributed function in a matched biological state can establish a compatible witness for that scoped function while its mechanistic explanation remains incomplete. Preserve the source's attribution and endpoint limits; a proxy phenotype alone establishes only what its experiment supports. Interpret unknown mechanistic details as limitations unless they leave an actual requirement of the declared claim unresolved.

Preserve the actual sample frame, weights, original opportunities and independent clusters. Technical repeats, time points and repeated representations do not create additional biological opportunities. Pair the necessary conditions on the same unit; do not multiply unpaired marginal fractions or assume a joint operating domain from favorable separate experiments. Narrow relation interpretation should answer the explicit biological proposition with supported, incompatible or unresolved meaning and source facts, never an overall plausibility percentage. Use available numerical measurements instead of replacing them with a verbal confidence grade.

Retain SD, SEM, untyped plus-minus spread, censoring and admissible model domains separately. Do not convert SD into a value interval, nondetection into zero, or a technical error-bar count into a context sampling denominator. Models identify experimental meanings, supported relations and operands; deterministic functions perform domain membership and numerical combinations. The retained-data population route does not imply that arbitrary literature or local-exposure calibration was automatically understood.

Use ordinary source operations and permitted narrower literature investigations to resolve the assigned question. Return only requested compatibility components, their actual context and sample meanings, uncertainty conditions and missing reasons. Logical bounds and conditional sampling intervals remain distinct. Source assay dependencies do not become another independent activity experiment, a second reliability multiplier, target correspondence or final annotation credit."""

A108_INVESTIGATION_TASK = """Investigate A108 organism and sample compatibility for the supplied material and biological question. Read supplied context sources to establish the caller's question and scope. Preserve that question when required observations are missing; describe the resulting uncertainty in its answer. Discover source-supported functional requirements and evidence about the actual organism, strain, compartment, environment or sample. Possible functions and organism identity may emerge from the evidence. Keep measured source facts separate from your assessment of their relevance to this target and question.

Your available work consists of the supplied literature and database search/acquisition operations, exact source text/table/figure readers, source-bound context assessment and final A108 publication, ordinary reasoning, and narrower literature investigations. The current catalog and selected operation contracts define the available actions. Choose further work according to the requirement or context uncertainty it can resolve. Database hits are leads; inspect original records and cited evidence. A missing result or failed request describes that acquisition, not a biological exclusion.

Publication queries retrieve indexed words rather than the complete biological proposition. Use discovered identities, functional names and individual contextual requirements as complementary search leads. When a long conjunction returns no relevant evidence, broaden or vary its terms and follow source citations as useful; requiring every detail of a supplied condition panel in one query can exclude relevant experiments. Keep an unresolved search distinct from a source that was read and found not to report the needed observation.

For a supplied protein sequence, public.literature.sequence_identity can retrieve records using its checksum and verify complete equality. Read source identifiers and organism information as attributed database statements; use discovered names and publications to investigate contextual evidence. The cited-publication metadata returned by public.literature.read links a paper's paragraph citations to its bibliography, supporting independent follow-up on reported physiological findings. An identifiable primary abstract can supply attributable observations at its stated level of detail; preserve its limited methods, conditions and uncertainty rather than inferring unreported details. source.locate supplies exact retained-source byte spans usable by readers. Read original tables when a text projection omits their headers or conditions. Distinct formats remain representations of the same observations.

Resolve each molecule's names within its organism, strain, locus, sequence and construct context. Distinguish a paper's investigated entity from its comparators and cited entities. Source-supported aliases can connect different names to the same molecule, while a shared name can designate different molecules in different organisms. Preserve the evidence for each correspondence and any remaining ambiguity before transferring observations or declaring an identity conflict.

Use literature.context.populate with source_selection for ordinary acquired sources. Set data_source_ref=null for this route. Establish the functional hypothesis through ordinary reasoning and bind its received reference and the supplied subject in question. The question rationale fixes organism capability or sample-context coverage before calculating the result. The settings record scope, frame, pairing, weights and sampling meaning with source witnesses. Requirement and route meanings cite their own definitions and function relationships. State observations use supported, incompatible or unresolved relations with an explicit interpretation and its source basis. Numeric observations and domain endpoints use source number and unit selectors; report unknowns when a required numerical reading is unsupported. Domain endpoint selection interprets a biological domain and requires evidence for that domain; separate favorable points do not establish the interval between them.

Keep one physical context per original unit and preserve source identity for shared observations. Use equal_unit weights only for an explicitly equally weighted frame; otherwise select reported weights under their actual basis. Preserve technical versus biological counts. Unknown context, joint support, scope, or unexamined permitted states remain explicit. Acquire complementary evidence when it can resolve those unknowns. An acquired paper and its database representation do not add another sample or experiment.

Save source-supported requirement_compatibility assessments and use literature.a108.finalize to publish the selected question's final compatibility result. Return the requested saved subscore cells, evidence relationships, conclusion and limitations through the parent's typed form. The same underlying evidence can yield useful bounds when a point is unavailable. The episode owns its source choices and the configured controller owns continuation; no required source order or reading quota is prescribed."""

__all__ = ["CONTEXT_TASK", "A108_INVESTIGATION_TASK"]
